# P18-V01 Remoting public surface slice — 2026-10-16 18:26 UTC

- Generated all-feature Remoting Rustdoc JSON with the installed nightly toolchain
  and enumerated the public inherent methods on `RemotingClient`. Before the
  change the scan found the public `invoke_name_server_with_peer`, which had no
  Java public operation counterpart and was only called by the response-only
  `invoke_name_server` wrapper. Commit `f853cb69` makes that implementation
  helper private and adds a compile-fail doctest.
- Updated the Phase 3 Remoting crosswalk with exact Rust method names for live
  connect-timeout and GO_AWAY setting adapters, both owned-processor methods,
  the private response-only helper, and the cross-crate sync peer adapter used
  by Core's NameServer route errors. The latest scan enumerates 64 public
  inherent methods and finds zero exact method names absent from the crosswalk.
- Verification on `f853cb69`: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, all-feature Remoting
  doctests (9), strict all-target/all-feature Remoting Clippy, and Core `rpc`
  route tests (5) pass. This closes a bounded Remoting method-name/public
  surface slice only; P18-V01 remains open for the full Java/Rust source,
  settings, overload/input/error/flow, inherited API, and reverse-export audit.

# P18-V01 Remoting semaphore helper API slice — 2026-10-16 18:41 UTC

- Pinned Java 5.5.1 exposes `SemaphoreReleaseOnlyOnce(Semaphore)`,
  `release()`, and `getSemaphore()`, plus two public `ResponseFuture` constructors.
  The Rust remoting crate now exposes `client::SemaphoreReleaseOnlyOnce` with
  nullable shared Tokio semaphore input, same-handle retrieval, and once-only
  release. `ResponseFuture::new` maps the null-helper constructor and
  `new_with_release_once` maps the helper constructor; the Tokio-only
  `new_with_permit` is private and guarded by a compile-fail doctest.
- Added `RemotingApiSurfaceFixtures` and
  `fixtures/remoting/response-future-api.json`, pinning both Java
  `ResponseFuture` constructors, all 20 declared methods, the helper
  constructor/methods, and repeated-release/null/identity outcomes. Fixture
  SHA-256: `4fc0509fee67637d2e1655a39dfb810ecac19e264289c6634448fa85f38aab4c`.
- Implementation commit: `978791b3`. Remoting all-feature tests pass (105 unit,
  8 codec, 1 fuzz, 7 security, 107 transport, 10 doctests); strict Remoting
  Clippy passes; formatting and diff checks pass. Pinned Maven `verify` passes
  with 37 scenarios and the reflection fixture. This closes only the helper and
  constructor slice; broad P18-V01 remains open and full-workspace gates on the
  eventual final revision are still due.
